WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.671
Let's build a simple retirement plan in MoneyWorks.

00:00:03.671 --> 00:00:09.068
We'll follow one example, from your starting point
to the savings you need.

00:00:10.529 --> 00:00:12.228
First, set your timeline.

00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:15.626
Enter your current age, your preferred retirement age,

00:00:15.626 --> 00:00:19.023
and how far ahead you want to plan.

00:00:20.707 --> 00:00:22.910
Next, add your monthly spending,

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:27.756
the portfolio you already have,
and what you save each month.

00:00:27.756 --> 00:00:30.840
Use the same currency for every amount.

00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:34.449
Now include a pension.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:38.030
Set the monthly payout and the ages it covers.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.622
Save closes the editor

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:42.805
and adds the payout to a compact list.

00:00:42.805 --> 00:00:46.386
You can use the pen to change it later.

00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:49.928
Choose Calculate.

00:00:49.928 --> 00:00:55.747
The retirement view shows the portfolio needed
at your chosen retirement age.

00:00:55.747 --> 00:01:02.050
The chart then follows that capital
as you spend and receive pension income.

00:01:04.622 --> 00:01:06.489
Switch to Savings plan.

00:01:06.489 --> 00:01:10.689
Here, compare your projected savings
with the retirement target.

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:17.222
If there's a gap, the calculator shows
the monthly saving needed to close it.

00:01:19.795 --> 00:01:24.558
Change an assumption and calculate again
to explore a different plan.

00:01:24.558 --> 00:01:28.889
Your inputs stay on this page;
they are not saved.
